lib/ - libcgra, the host C library
==================================

The host half of the CGRA. Owns the serial transport, the v2/v3 protocols, the
accelerated kernels, and an in-process emulator that speaks the identical wire
protocol so the whole stack runs with no FPGA.

Layout
------
    include/    public API - cgra.h (the only header you include)
    src/        transport, vector/tiled kernels, emulator and PTY server
    test/       assert.h unit tests (TAP output), run against sim:
    doc/        man page (libcgra.3), hand-written, groff -man
    cgra.pc.in  pkg-config template (installed as cgra.pc, see root `make install`)

Build (make -f lib.mk <target>)
-------------------------------
    all                  build/libcgra.a + build/libcgra.so* (static + shared)
    test                 build + run the unit tests (assertions forced on)
    PROFILE=asan test    tests under AddressSanitizer + UBSan
    valgrind             tests under valgrind
    analyze              gcc -fanalyzer static analysis
    man                  lint + render doc/libcgra.3 -> build/libcgra.3.txt
    clean

Build profiles (PROFILE=...): release (default, -O3 -DNDEBUG), debug (-O0 -g3),
asan, ubsan. Diagnostics are strict everywhere (-Wall -Wextra -Wconversion
-Wshadow -Wcast-qual ... ; see WARN in lib.mk).

Link against it with: cc ... -Iinclude -Llib/build -lcgra
Installed, prefer pkg-config: cc ... $(pkg-config --cflags --libs cgra)

Quick taste
-----------
    cgra_t *d = cgra_open("sim:", 115200);      /* no hardware needed */
    int16_t a[4]={1,2,3,4}, b[4]={10,20,30,40}, out[4];
    cgra_vec_add(d, a, b, out, 4);              /* -> 11 22 33 44 */
    cgra_close(d);

Docs
----
The API is documented in include/cgra.h (Unix-style block comments, no
doxygen) and in doc/libcgra.3. See also the CLI: cgra(1), cgra(5).

Installed kernels: cgra_vec_*, cgra_dot, cgra_matvec, cgra_scan, cgra_conv.
All adapt to the device geometry and return CGRA_OK or a negative error.
Matrix/scan/convolution take size_t dimensions and output capacities. They
are shared with the CLI, without any DSL dependency in the library.
See the header for empty inputs, exact in-place vector/scan use, rejected
overlap, partial output on failure, ownership and synchronization contracts.

Contract
--------
The protocol bytes and config-word layout are shared with hw/rtl/cgra_pkg.vhd.
src/emu.c is the golden reference the RTL testbenches are checked against -
keep header, emulator and VHDL package in lockstep.

Serial descriptors are close-on-exec; cgra_open_ex optionally requests
exclusive access. cgra_set_timeout retains its response-only contract;
cgra_set_transaction_timeout adds a shared write/reply/retry budget per wire
command. cgra_get_diagnostic copies the last failed command's phase, errno
and partial progress without borrowed data. See the header for exact scope.
cgra_emulate_pty_ex selects geometry/version and a borrowed cancellation fd.
The model has no clock and does not model the RTL parser watchdog.

Reusable plans
--------------
cgra_plan_create owns and pre-serializes a CFG plus geometry/steps/flags/taps.
cgra_plan_bind loads it explicitly; cgra_plan_execute_n then reuses the known
configuration for repeated inputs on v2/v3. Raw wire commands invalidate the
binding, as do failed transfers. STALE requires an explicit bind; DESYNC
still requires parser/session recovery. There is no implicit reload/cache.
Plans do not borrow caller config arrays and handles do not borrow plans.
See libcgra(3) and test/test_plans.c for usage, ownership and stateful examples.

Bit-vector arithmetic uses unsigned intermediates and explicit in-range
conversion to int16_t. Arithmetic right shifts use explicit sign extension;
they do not depend on the C compiler's treatment of negative signed shifts.
Optional instrumentation
    cgra_set_profiling / cgra_get_profile add monotonic host I/O timing without
    changing cgra_stats_t. CFG time is separate from other transport calls;
    serial waits and emulator work are included. Disabled by default. This
    does not measure FPGA compute latency; see libcgra(3) for counter semantics.
